      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5f09292295ffa944efa05d41",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I'm OK with 8 controls (or maybe up to 10 if not the root) per radial menu, but I wish there was an alternative submenu format that avatar makers can use for lists that would contain up to more than 8-10 options that don't need to be accessed quickly, such as lists of animations (actions). The obvious choice would be a scrollable vertical menu. Thumbstick up-down to scroll through the menu. Thumbstick left to highlight a \"back\" button from anywhere in the menu. Thumbstick right to go back to the list of options. Trigger to activate/toggle. This menu type would only support \"button\", \"toggle\", \"submenu\" and \"back\".",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-11T02:51:14.467Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It is currently possible to expand the number of controls per expression menu beyond 8 with the Unity debug inspector.  The in-game menu works and can comfortably fit more than 8 items.  It would be nice if this cap was raised to something higher or removed entirely.",
